1
00:00:01,250 --> 00:00:04,000
ALLEN: 8 YEARS OLD

2
00:00:01,250 --> 00:00:04,000
LATE DECEMBER

3
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:09,380
How scrumptious. What sort of meat is in this?

4
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:12,330
Horned rabbit meat. Allen hunted them!

5
00:00:12,710 --> 00:00:15,880
Oh? I'd expect nothing less from Rodin's son.

6
00:00:16,210 --> 00:00:20,920
Speaking of, I hear that Krena Village has
successfully met their quota of 20 great boars.

7
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:22,540
That's great news.

8
00:00:22,540 --> 00:00:25,080
No surprise. I never doubted Dad for a second.

9
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:28,250
Then why haven't we had any for dinner this year?

10
00:00:28,670 --> 00:00:31,210
Great boar used to be a highlight
of our winter meals.

11
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:34,790
Good point. Did they all get sent
to the royal capital?

12
00:00:34,790 --> 00:00:37,330
The King was the one who ordered
we hunt more, after all.

13
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:39,170
Don't be selfish, son.

14
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:40,880
Sorry...

15
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:43,330
Harsh!

16
00:00:43,330 --> 00:00:46,750
It's crazy to think serfs eat more meat
than the son of a noble.

17
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:49,790
Still, it's unfortunate we don't have
any boar meat to serve.

18
00:00:49,790 --> 00:00:52,290
It will put a damper
on the new year's festivities.

19
00:00:52,710 --> 00:00:54,960
Yes, well, there's not much we can do.

20
00:00:55,250 --> 00:00:56,330
Hey, Allen?

21
00:00:56,330 --> 00:00:57,080
Yes?

22
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:00,080
Hunt a white deer next time, would you?

23
00:01:00,080 --> 00:01:04,000
Elder brother! You have to go through me
to give Allen orders!

24
00:01:04,250 --> 00:01:05,920
What is she, my talent agent?

25
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:09,380
Thomas, you silly boy.
That's a tall order for Allen.

26
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:10,750
Very well.

27
00:01:11,540 --> 00:01:13,880
I shall hunt you a white deer.

28
00:01:15,750 --> 00:01:16,960
Hooray!

29
00:01:17,670 --> 00:01:22,380
White deer, eh? Pretty sure it's
a C-rank monster just like the boars.

30
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:24,710
And I love me a challenge!

31
00:02:56,540 --> 00:03:00,630
EPISODE 8: HUNTSMAN

32
00:03:03,830 --> 00:03:05,580
Did you find what I asked you to?

33
00:03:09,630 --> 00:03:10,580
Bingo!

34
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:16,080
I've seen them from a distance before,
but white deer are huge up close.

35
00:03:16,710 --> 00:03:18,290
Hopper squad, you're up!

36
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:21,000
Use Provoke!

37
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:30,330
Ribbit, ribbit, ribbit, ribbit.

38
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:31,880
Okay, return!

39
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:33,630
Now!

40
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,210
Hopper squad, do it again!

41
00:03:35,330 --> 00:03:37,960
Ribbit, ribbit, ribbit, ribbit.

42
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:38,750
Return!

43
00:03:39,250 --> 00:03:42,460
Ribbit, ribbit, ribbit, ribbit.

44
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:45,920
Ribbit, ribbit, ribbit, ribbit.

45
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,210
Ribbit, ribbit, ribbit.

46
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:50,330
Nailed it!

47
00:03:54,380 --> 00:03:57,790
The key to being a Summoner
is knowing how to abuse your summons!

48
00:03:58,290 --> 00:04:00,420
Now, meet your maker!

49
00:04:02,380 --> 00:04:04,170
M-monster at the gates!

50
00:04:08,790 --> 00:04:10,290
Wh-what the heck?

51
00:04:10,630 --> 00:04:12,540
How did it even get in here?!

52
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:14,250
Take me to...

53
00:04:15,420 --> 00:04:17,580
Master Thomas...

54
00:04:17,710 --> 00:04:19,250
The monster can talk?!

55
00:04:20,290 --> 00:04:22,710
Ugh, this weighs a ton!

56
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:29,460
I went hunting for Master Thomas.
This white deer is for him.

57
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:31,580
M-my goodness!

58
00:04:31,580 --> 00:04:32,880
Wow, a white deer!

59
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:34,330
Amazing...

60
00:04:34,330 --> 00:04:37,960
Look, Mother! Now we have something special
to serve at the new year's party!

61
00:04:38,710 --> 00:04:40,170
Yes, I suppose we do.

62
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:42,500
Thank you, Allen!

63
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:43,750
You're most welcome.

64
00:04:44,170 --> 00:04:48,000
This oversized pain in the butt totally
isn't worth the 2,500 EXP that it gives.

65
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,670
I'm never hunting one again!

66
00:04:50,170 --> 00:04:53,960
Tell me, Sebas. Are we certain he has no talent?

67
00:04:54,380 --> 00:04:57,040
Because I don't understand how an eight year old
can hunt C-rank monsters like this.

68
00:04:57,210 --> 00:04:58,750
You must reinvestigate immediately.

69
00:04:58,750 --> 00:04:59,710
Yessir.

70
00:05:01,290 --> 00:05:02,460
Huntsman?

71
00:05:03,250 --> 00:05:06,380
That's right. In light of
your recent accomplishments,

72
00:05:06,380 --> 00:05:09,420
we've decided to assign you a new position.

73
00:05:09,670 --> 00:05:11,880
The huntsman has two duties:

74
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:15,630
First, hunting monsters
to provide food for the family.

75
00:05:15,630 --> 00:05:19,080
And second, rescuing townsfolk
from any monster attacks.

76
00:05:19,380 --> 00:05:22,130
Basically, a hunter employed by the baron.

77
00:05:22,290 --> 00:05:23,670
Wow.

78
00:05:23,670 --> 00:05:27,880
So, like, I can just go hunting for monsters
every day and call it work?

79
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,130
Of course, we don't expect you to do it for free.

80
00:05:30,250 --> 00:05:34,580
You will receive 100 silver coins,
which is double your current monthly wage.

81
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:36,210
I see.

82
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:41,170
They'd rather give me a fixed salary instead
of paying per monster like they did before.

83
00:05:41,380 --> 00:05:45,330
Since a white deer is definitely worth
more than 100 silver coins.

84
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:47,880
Hm? Not to your liking?

85
00:05:48,080 --> 00:05:49,750
No! It sounds great!

86
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:52,750
This is the best deal I could ask for!

87
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:56,080
All I have to do is hunt enough monsters
to provide the necessary meat,

88
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:58,540
then I'm free to spend
the rest of my time farming goblins!

89
00:05:58,540 --> 00:06:00,460
Man! I'm practically drooling at the thought!

90
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:04,290
I understand. I'll gladly take on
the title of huntsman.

91
00:06:04,540 --> 00:06:06,040
I'll get started tomorrow...

92
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:08,920
Hold it. Nobody said you would work every day.

93
00:06:09,170 --> 00:06:09,750
Huh?

94
00:06:09,750 --> 00:06:14,420
Naturally, you must also continue
being Lady Cecil's manservant.

95
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:20,380
Not to mention your waiter duties. You will only
need to work as a huntsman once a week or so.

96
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:21,540
Okay...

97
00:06:21,830 --> 00:06:24,380
Your feelings are always written on your face.

98
00:06:24,630 --> 00:06:28,540
I can just shelve this whole idea
if you find it so upsetting.

99
00:06:28,540 --> 00:06:29,710
N-no, sir!

100
00:06:29,830 --> 00:06:31,790
I shall humbly carry out all my duties.

101
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:34,790
Aw crap! I shouldn't look
a gift horse in the mouth!

102
00:06:36,210 --> 00:06:39,250
MARCH OF THE NEW YEAR

103
00:06:39,420 --> 00:06:40,710
That's his ship!

104
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:43,830
It's quite a sight to behold up close.

105
00:06:44,330 --> 00:06:48,380
I get that it's powered by magic stones,
but what exactly makes it float?

106
00:06:48,880 --> 00:06:51,330
Don't let it slip that I baked him cookies, okay?

107
00:06:51,540 --> 00:06:54,040
I want him to be surprised!

108
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:56,630
But of course, milady.

109
00:07:01,170 --> 00:07:02,580
Elder Brother!

110
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:04,130
Hey, Cecil!

111
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:06,830
Welcome back, Mihai!

112
00:07:06,830 --> 00:07:08,210
How have you been?

113
00:07:08,210 --> 00:07:10,750
I've been great! Except for how much I missed you!

114
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,130
So, is that good or bad?

115
00:07:13,290 --> 00:07:16,420
You broke your promise to come visit
during summer vacation.

116
00:07:16,670 --> 00:07:18,880
You're right. I'm sorry.

117
00:07:19,290 --> 00:07:21,540
Well, they seem to get along well.

118
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:26,000
Given that he started attending the Academy
last year, he must be turning 14 soon.

119
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:28,290
But he looks older than that.

120
00:07:28,960 --> 00:07:31,170
Allow me to take your luggage, milord.

121
00:07:32,210 --> 00:07:34,460
You must be one of the newer servants.

122
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:37,420
Yes. I have been serving
the family since last fall.

123
00:07:37,670 --> 00:07:38,920
My name is Allen.

124
00:07:38,920 --> 00:07:41,290
He's doing double duty as manservant and huntsman!

125
00:07:41,580 --> 00:07:43,330
Wow! At such a young age?

126
00:07:49,880 --> 00:07:52,330
I can tell you must be very gifted, Allen!

127
00:07:52,710 --> 00:07:56,630
Not at all. I owe it
to Lady Cecil's gracious favor.

128
00:07:56,880 --> 00:07:58,830
He's clearly the mature one of the bunch.

129
00:07:59,630 --> 00:08:00,380
Oh, right.

130
00:08:00,670 --> 00:08:03,000
Here. A souvenir from the capital.

131
00:08:03,420 --> 00:08:06,330
Wow! Thank you!

132
00:08:06,330 --> 00:08:08,380
I'll treasure it forever!

133
00:08:09,540 --> 00:08:13,460
C'mon! Let's go home so you can regale me
with stories of your time at the Academy!

134
00:08:13,580 --> 00:08:15,710
There are yummy cookies waiting for us!

135
00:08:15,710 --> 00:08:17,920
Oh? That sounds wonderful.

136
00:08:19,790 --> 00:08:22,170
I hope Mash and Myulla are doing okay back home.

137
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:27,250
Gotcha!

138
00:08:29,670 --> 00:08:31,920
Nice. That fills my quota.

139
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:33,790
Time to pack it in for the day.

140
00:08:34,460 --> 00:08:36,250
Shucks, Allen!

141
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:37,750
Another big haul today!

142
00:08:37,750 --> 00:08:38,380
Wow.

143
00:08:38,380 --> 00:08:40,420
You even got the big toad I asked for!

144
00:08:40,420 --> 00:08:41,500
Of course, Head Chef!

145
00:08:41,670 --> 00:08:44,790
This will put a smile
on Master Mihai's face for sure.

146
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:49,710
Guess what, Allen? Master Mihai and Sir Zenoff
are actually having a duel right now!

147
00:09:00,880 --> 00:09:04,580
Wow! This is the first time I've seen
Sir Zenoff using his sword.

148
00:09:04,830 --> 00:09:07,420
Mihai's really holding his own against him.

149
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:11,500
Let's leave it at that.

150
00:09:12,460 --> 00:09:16,460
Your skills have become much sharper
in the past year, young lad.

151
00:09:16,670 --> 00:09:17,670
Thank you.

152
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:20,920
Though I think I've outgrown
being called a "young lad."

153
00:09:23,880 --> 00:09:25,750
Oh, Allen. You're back?

154
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:28,210
That's quite the haul.

155
00:09:28,380 --> 00:09:30,000
Impressive, Allen!

156
00:09:30,290 --> 00:09:33,710
Since you're so tough,
I'd love to spar with you for a bit.

157
00:09:33,920 --> 00:09:35,880
Huh? Are you sure?

158
00:09:40,130 --> 00:09:40,920
Here, Allen.

159
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:44,170
Thank you, sir.

160
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:47,790
A mithril sword! Badass!

161
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:50,670
Man, I haven't sparred with
anybody since I parted ways with Krena.

