212
00:10:00,540 --> 00:10:01,960
I bet I can win!

213
00:10:03,170 --> 00:10:04,500
At the ready.

214
00:10:10,710 --> 00:10:11,290
Begin!

215
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,000
Hafta be careful not to hurt him.

216
00:10:17,540 --> 00:10:18,130
Here I come!

217
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:23,670
Um, he hits like a truck. Seems kinda OP.

218
00:10:23,880 --> 00:10:25,500
Fine! Let me bust out my speed on him.

219
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:27,290
Wait, he's faster than me, too?!

220
00:10:30,750 --> 00:10:33,330
That feel when you get parried like a total scrub.

221
00:10:38,670 --> 00:10:39,500
Mihai...

222
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:42,420
Have no fear, my lady.

223
00:10:42,710 --> 00:10:43,290
Huh?

224
00:10:43,670 --> 00:10:48,250
Master Mihai has spent a whole year undergoing
training in the renowned Academy City.

225
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:52,000
There is no chance he loses
to someone without that experience.

226
00:10:57,380 --> 00:10:59,290
I admit defeat.

227
00:10:59,880 --> 00:11:00,630
Wow!

228
00:11:00,630 --> 00:11:02,130
So cool!

229
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:05,830
I can certainly see how you made
manservant at your age!

230
00:11:06,330 --> 00:11:08,500
Thank you... milord.

231
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,630
He's in a whole different league!

232
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:11,920
I never stood a chance.

233
00:11:12,170 --> 00:11:14,130
Amazing, Elder Brother!

234
00:11:14,420 --> 00:11:17,500
I'll give you some credit, Allen.
You weren't half-bad, either.

235
00:11:17,670 --> 00:11:19,170
Why, thank you.

236
00:11:19,460 --> 00:11:21,130
Who died and made you Queen?!

237
00:11:21,460 --> 00:11:24,080
You're so much stronger than you were last year.

238
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:26,830
Well, that's because I cleared
a dungeon over the summer.

239
00:11:26,830 --> 00:11:27,880
Dungeon?

240
00:11:28,330 --> 00:11:30,540
It's like a maze where you fight monsters.

241
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:33,880
I needed to clear it
or I would've gotten expelled.

242
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:38,080
Really?! No wonder you couldn't
come home over the summer.

243
00:11:38,290 --> 00:11:42,000
Clearing a dungeon
for summer homework? That's sick!

244
00:11:42,130 --> 00:11:44,080
Life at the Academy is rough, but it's worth it.

245
00:11:44,080 --> 00:11:46,710
For example, I had the opportunity
to learn the intricacies of swordsmanship

246
00:11:46,710 --> 00:11:48,540
from Dverg the Sword Lord.

247
00:11:48,630 --> 00:11:50,830
Wow, from Lord Dverg himself?!

248
00:11:51,040 --> 00:11:53,790
Neat. Sounds like a stacked teaching staff.

249
00:11:54,170 --> 00:11:56,460
That's amazing! What was he like?

250
00:11:56,630 --> 00:11:58,040
Hm, how can I put it...

251
00:11:58,290 --> 00:12:02,170
Now I get it. He trained
with Sword Lords and cleared dungeons.

252
00:12:02,460 --> 00:12:05,630
Plus, being on normal mode
means that he progresses 100 times faster

253
00:12:05,630 --> 00:12:07,130
than I do on Hell Mode.

254
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:09,750
So this is how strong
someone with a talent can get

255
00:12:09,750 --> 00:12:11,830
by dedicating a whole year to leveling up, huh?

256
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:16,380
Tell me, Mihai! When will you come visit us again?

257
00:12:16,380 --> 00:12:18,250
Not until summer of next year, most likely.

258
00:12:18,250 --> 00:12:19,630
Boo...

259
00:12:19,920 --> 00:12:22,210
Please spar with me again when you do!

260
00:12:24,420 --> 00:12:25,330
Sure thing.

261
00:12:25,750 --> 00:12:27,880
But take good care of my sister
while I'm away, would you?

262
00:12:28,630 --> 00:12:29,460
Sound good, Allen?

263
00:12:30,460 --> 00:12:32,830
Uh, yeah.

264
00:12:33,330 --> 00:12:34,830
Screw that.

265
00:12:34,830 --> 00:12:38,330
I'm trying to rise the servant ranks
and make a name for myself.

266
00:12:38,330 --> 00:12:40,630
If I had my way, I'd be out hunting every day!

267
00:12:41,080 --> 00:12:43,920
I'm doomed to serve Cecil forever at this rate!

268
00:12:44,460 --> 00:12:49,290
I gotta figure out a way to quit this gig
without shaming my dad in the process...

269
00:12:53,040 --> 00:12:56,630
A few days later,
Mihai left to return to Academy City.

270
00:12:57,540 --> 00:13:00,710
That's where Krena, Dogora,
and eventually Cecil will go.

271
00:13:01,880 --> 00:13:04,750
Dungeons sound fun. Wish I could clear one.

272
00:13:08,080 --> 00:13:10,290
I'm not crying and these are not tears, got it?!

273
00:13:11,630 --> 00:13:12,830
Uh, sure.

274
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:18,080
THE HARDCORE GAMER DOMINATES

275
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:18,080
IN ANOTHER WORLD WITH GARBAGE BALANCING

276
00:13:18,420 --> 00:13:22,040
ALLEN: AGE 8

277
00:13:18,420 --> 00:13:22,040
EARLY APRIL

278
00:13:19,210 --> 00:13:21,920
It's an honor to have you, Viscount Carnel.

279
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:24,670
Think nothing of it, Baron Granvelle!

280
00:13:24,790 --> 00:13:29,210
Sometimes it can be nice to enjoy
the quaint landscapes of the lifeless backcountry.

281
00:13:29,420 --> 00:13:31,830
Oh really. How wonderful.

282
00:13:43,290 --> 00:13:44,960
Rickel was explaining to me earlier...

283
00:13:45,540 --> 00:13:46,960
Viscount Carnel?

284
00:13:47,250 --> 00:13:50,460
He's in charge of the neighboring fiefdom,
on the other side of the White Dragon Mountains.

285
00:13:50,670 --> 00:13:53,750
The viscount is one rank higher
in social status over the baron.

286
00:13:54,130 --> 00:13:57,380
Why the sudden visit?
Does he have important business here?

287
00:13:57,790 --> 00:14:01,630
Dunno. But I heard he took a magic ship all
the way from the royal capital just to drop by.

288
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,170
Better watch out.

289
00:14:03,330 --> 00:14:08,130
The Granvelles and the Carnels have been
at each other's throats for centuries.

290
00:14:11,170 --> 00:14:12,250
Superb!

291
00:14:12,420 --> 00:14:15,170
This must be the boar meat
I've heard so much about!

292
00:14:15,170 --> 00:14:16,710
Indeed it is. Right, Allen?

293
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:18,290
Y-yessir.

294
00:14:18,540 --> 00:14:20,750
He knows full well it's just horned rabbit.

295
00:14:21,170 --> 00:14:23,830
Don't want to waste any boar meat
on this joker, huh?

296
00:14:24,250 --> 00:14:29,000
I see. No wonder you wanted
to keep this tasty morsel a secret!

297
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:32,460
It was by no means a secret.

298
00:14:32,920 --> 00:14:35,460
Man, he's really pissed. But it's only fair.

299
00:14:35,750 --> 00:14:36,710
That scoundrel!

300
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:39,960
Calling attention to the boar hunts
while we're in front of the King!

301
00:14:40,130 --> 00:14:43,250
This jerk is the one who
spilled the beans to the King

302
00:14:43,250 --> 00:14:45,130
and caused a fuss over the boar meat quota.

303
00:14:45,130 --> 00:14:47,710
Now it all has to go to the royal capital.

304
00:14:48,750 --> 00:14:50,210
I'd like a second serving.

305
00:14:50,580 --> 00:14:51,880
Right away, sir.

306
00:14:52,790 --> 00:14:57,380
Your fiefdom is already better off.
Stop punching down, asshole.

307
00:14:57,750 --> 00:15:01,420
HISTORY LESSONS

308
00:14:57,750 --> 00:15:01,420
WITH RICKEL

309
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:01,580
History Lessons with Rickel!

310
00:15:01,830 --> 00:15:03,500
Let's get started.

311
00:15:03,710 --> 00:15:11,670
CARNEL FIEFDOM

312
00:15:03,710 --> 00:15:11,670
GRANVELLE FIEFDOM

313
00:15:03,710 --> 00:15:11,670
WHITE DRAGON MOUNTAINS

314
00:15:04,210 --> 00:15:07,960
The White Dragon Mountains
are filled with mithril deposits.

315
00:15:08,290 --> 00:15:11,080
There are multiple mines in both territories,

316
00:15:11,330 --> 00:15:14,290
but because the white dragon
has made its nest on this side,

317
00:15:14,630 --> 00:15:16,420
we can't access any of ours.

318
00:15:17,630 --> 00:15:21,330
That's why the Granvelle Fiefdom
is going through an economic downturn, huh?

319
00:15:21,710 --> 00:15:23,790
Thankfully, the white dragon is pretty fickle,

320
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:27,380
so it switches to roost on the other side
every hundred years.

321
00:15:27,790 --> 00:15:32,290
Hence, about a century ago, it was the
Carnel Fiefdom that was struggling instead.

322
00:15:32,290 --> 00:15:33,880
I see!

323
00:15:34,170 --> 00:15:36,000
Not an easy problem to solve.

324
00:15:36,170 --> 00:15:39,830
Back then, the Granvelle Fiefdom
might have been the bully.

325
00:15:41,460 --> 00:15:43,290
So, what brings you here today?

326
00:15:43,670 --> 00:15:47,000
I can't imagine you came all this way
just to eat boar meat.

327
00:15:47,210 --> 00:15:49,170
Ah, yes. Of course.

328
00:15:49,330 --> 00:15:51,790
The boar meat was so tasty that I almost forgot.

329
00:15:51,790 --> 00:15:53,380
That's horned rabbit, my dude.

330
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:57,790
A few days ago, my youngest daughter
underwent the Appraisal Ceremony.

331
00:15:57,790 --> 00:16:00,000
I came here to share the results.

332
00:16:00,330 --> 00:16:02,630
Oh, it's already that time of year?

333
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:05,330
I really hope Mash has a talent.

334
00:16:05,330 --> 00:16:07,290
He was good with a spear.

335
00:16:05,540 --> 00:16:07,830
TALENT: SPEAR USER

336
00:16:08,170 --> 00:16:09,920
Well, let's hear it.

337
00:16:10,170 --> 00:16:13,130
Fortunately, she's talentless!

338
00:16:16,250 --> 00:16:19,330
Huh? Their reactions don't make sense to me.

339
00:16:19,790 --> 00:16:25,920
It's such a shame, Baron Granvelle.
Two of your three kids got saddled with a talent.

340
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:29,130
I seem to recall your eldest son
also had a talent, Viscount!

341
00:16:29,630 --> 00:16:33,130
You know how it goes.
We must fulfill the noble's duty.

342
00:16:36,210 --> 00:16:38,880
How is having a talent a bad thing?

343
00:16:39,330 --> 00:16:41,880
Why come all this way on a ship
just to rub that in his face?

344
00:16:42,630 --> 00:16:46,290
The commoners and serfs who I know
were all overjoyed to have a talent.

345
00:16:46,540 --> 00:16:49,080
Is there some kind of downside to it for nobles?

346
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:53,380
Such tasty boar, simply ham-tacular.

347
00:16:51,130 --> 00:16:53,380
What is this "noble's duty"
they were talking about?

348
00:16:54,460 --> 00:16:57,630
Gotta say, being a noble seems like it sucks.

349
00:16:58,630 --> 00:17:00,630
ALLEN: AGE 9

350
00:16:58,630 --> 00:17:00,630
EARLY OCTOBER

351
00:16:58,630 --> 00:17:00,630
ALLEN'S DAY OFF

352
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:02,920
So, you've got the day off?

353
00:17:03,460 --> 00:17:08,040
Yeah. I'm actually considering doing my hunting
a little farther away from town.

354
00:17:08,080 --> 00:17:11,580
So I was wondering if you would share your
knowledge about C-rank monsters with me.

355
00:17:13,580 --> 00:17:15,540
I've taken down roughly
10,000 goblins at this point.

356
00:17:15,750 --> 00:17:18,880
There's hardly any left to hunt around here.

